+# Validation Sprint Runbook: Drift → Retrain → Canary (Staged Validation)
+
+Objective:
+- Execute a 2–4 week staged validation sprint to prove the drift→retrain→canary flow end‑to‑end on a real model/dataset, collect evidence, and iterate on hardening issues.
+
+Scope:
+- One model family, one dataset. Use staging cluster, real provider credentials if available (no paid QPU usage without legal signoff).
+
+Prereqs:
+- Tekton pipeline `drift-retrain-canary-pipeline` installed.
+- Drift detector deployed and configured with baseline/latest sample URIs.
+- Evidence S3 bucket configured (EVIDENCE_BUCKET) and accessible by CI/pipelines.
+- OTEL collector + Prometheus running and reachable.
+- Labeling UI (Label Studio) deployed for active learning (optional).
+- Redis instance for rate limiter (optional).
+
+Phases:
+1) Preparation (Day 0)
+ - Select model & dataset; snapshot baseline dataset (S3 path) and ensure latest sample ingestion.
+ - Configure DRIFT_THRESHOLD conservatively (e.g. 0.05).
+ - Ensure cosign key and KMS access; store key in secret mount for pipeline.
+ - Create pipeline-approvals ConfigMap in cicd namespace and set approved=false.
+
+2) Dry runs (Days 1–3)
+ - Run `services/quantum/live_e2e_runner.py --run-tests` to sanity-check provider adapters (if used).
+ - Trigger Tekton pipeline manually for a single retrain; validate all tasks succeed and evidence is uploaded.
+ - Review Great Expectations and other validation outputs.
+
+3) Controlled stress & canary validation (Days 4–10)
+ - Run Tekton `validation-sprint-pipeline` repeatedly (1–2 runs/day) with simulated traffic to canary service.
+ - Run the `qpu-stress` task if testing QPU submission scale impacts (careful with cost).
+ - Collect traces using OTEL; run `services/quantum/worker_postmortem_helpers.py` after each run for artifacts.
+
+4) Active learning (Days 7–21)
+ - Use Label Studio to label edge cases; integrate labeled batches via Tekton `labeling-ingest-task`.
+ - Re-run retrain pipeline using new labeled data and compare metrics.
+
+5) Acceptance & long-shadow (Day 14+)
+ - After N successful runs and SME signoffs, start long-shadow mode: route a % of live traffic to canary while collecting metrics for 30 days or run accelerated simulations.
+ - Configure Canary controller thresholds and Prometheus alerting.
+
+Deliverables:
+- Evidence S3 path with all artifacts.
+- Postmortem report with issues and fixes.
+- SME signoffs uploaded to s3://<EVIDENCE_BUCKET>/signoffs/
+- Checklist marking components hardened or requiring further work.
+
